+# Veterinarian Search Narrowed to a Specialty Filter
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for pets, visits, and veterinarians, leaving owners the only searchable entity. Like every row but NG-4 and NG-5, it was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty arrived on 2026-08-30. Read whole, NG-9 refused it. Read narrowly, NG-9 refused only free-text search and left an attribute filter untouched. The boundary had to settle which reading binds.
+
+The owner decided the row on 2026-08-30: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, and filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows comes in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Refuse the filter as veterinarian search. Rejected: the row's stated reason is that owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search. A whole-name filter on an attribute the page already prints does not repeat that demonstration.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open veterinarian search generally. Rejected: free-text search over veterinarians would add the surface the row was written to keep out, and pets and visits stay unsearchable regardless.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to one named specialty is in scope and is recorded as REQ-VET-004. Searching veterinarians by name or by free text remains declined, as does search over pets and visits.
+
+The narrowing is asked for in the request. Neither directory form gains a page control under this decision; a visible control is a separate request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- REQ-VET-004 records the filter across both directory forms. REQ-VET-003 records the machine-readable form as a supported surface.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation. Every row but NG-4, NG-5, and NG-9 remains part of it.
+- Filtering another listing by an attribute it already shows is not thereby licensed. Each such request takes its own owner decision.
+- REQ-VET-002 stays withdrawn and its id is not reused. REQ-VET-003 is a new decision, not a reversal of the 2026-07-31 record.
+- NG-2 is untouched: reading the directory is not managing veterinarians or their specialties.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble naming it decided.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-004) — the filter requirement and its acceptance.
